{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CI triage (Gerrit 2416 Verified-1, patchset 1): the public-surface drift gate\n(tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py) failed on all 3 Python versions because\nadding pinned_ticket_read_failed to KNOWN_ERROR_CODES changed the pinned public\nconstant rebar.KNOWN_ERROR_CODES, and the committed baseline\ntests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json was stale. Not a flake (deterministic across\npy3.11/3.12/3.13). Fix: regenerated the baseline via\n`python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --update` (exactly one added line,\n'pinned_ticket_read_failed') and folded it into this change via a scripted\nrebase-edit of the 0aee commit (Change-Id preserved), replaying the 5f96 and\nguardrail commits on top. Local `--check` and full test_api_surface_gate.py (14)\nnow pass. Re-pushed as patchset 2."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788072187805679001,"uuid":"f37923b4-d268-43e4-a99d-ca1be129e99f"}